{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1189858-the-early-20th-century-the-sons-of-ether-and-the-ahl-i-batin","id":1189858,"title":"The Early 20th Century, the Sons of Ether and the Ahl-i-Batin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-27T07:31:04-08:00","id":1189858,"title":"The Early 20th Century, the Sons of Ether and the Ahl-i-Batin","content":"So, the Electrodyne Engineers defected from the Technocracy and changed their name to the Sons of Ether in 1904.<br /> <br /> The Ahl-i-Batin formally resigned from the Council of Nine Mystick Traditions in either 1922 or 1932 (I've read conflicting sources on that).<br /> <br /> That means that the Batini and the Etherites had either 18 or 28 years on the Council together. What were their relationships like? How did they perceive eachother? Did they ever collaborate?<br /> <br /> Personally, I suspect the Etherites joining the Traditions might have been the straw that broke the camel's back for the Batini. Their hatred for the Technocracy is well noted, so accepting a bunch of technomancers was bad enough, but worse, they were radically individualistic and some of the least subtle willworkers this side of the Taftani.<br /> <br /> On the Etherite side, I think the reaction is a bit more charitable. After all, the Batini have historically been philosopher scientists and their own parent culture literally wrote the book on dynamic Science (the Kitab al-Alacir). Of course, the extremely Eurocentric mindset the early Etherites held probably strained relations.<br /> <br /> Anybody else agree or disagree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 02-27-2018, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:13:45-08:00","id":1189885,"title":"","content":"Whereas these two factions hadn't enough time to get to know each other, it is possible that they had quarrels. Etherites were eccentric daring-do types long before joining the Coiuncil. They were always the type of fellow to seek conflict.<br /> Middle east was a focus of conflict over Batini Nodes (the Web of Faith), and if you mix that with the fact that the Kitab al-Alacir was written there, it makes sense to think that more than one Electrodyne Engineer would sign to go there and take part in the conflict. If Etherites killed Batini, took a few Nodes by force, and then became &quot;untouchable&quot; because they're among the Traditions now, that would have stirred political conflict that would add to the other problems they had with the Council.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:32:08-08:00","id":1189893,"title":"","content":"I imagine the Etherites were generally received with a large dose of suspicion from all sides when they first arrived. While the Etherites themselves were probably a mix of those who weren\u2019t overly keen on the traditions themselves, perhaps seeing them as inherently unscientific thinkers with no imagination beyond whatever dogma they happened to adhere to.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what would be different about the batini that would make this particular relationship so strained, but then differing opinions on colonialism may have had a factor into things.<br /> <br /> I imagine many Etherites, especially at the time,to be fairly colonialist in ethos, something that would have particularly rubbed up a few tradition members the wrong way, especially the Akashics, Dreamspeaker, and the Batini. Who, outside the crafts, probably had the most to lose from colonialisation. Possibly the Euthanatos too, but I\u2019m not sure.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the Dreamspeakers were too fractured have a unified voice against them, while the Akashics might have been a bit more forgiving, or at the very least less grudgebaring. If the Euthanatos, especially the African and Indian Euthanatos, held any ill will towards them, it may have been tempred by their understanding of fate.<br /> <br /> I can imagine the batini becoming more inward looking in response to the Etherites presence, perhaps to the point of separatism. But I don\u2019t think the Etherites were the straw so much, but rather that it was because the traditions didn\u2019t prioritise protecting the Middle East. The Batini left to preserve the Web of Faith, because they could no longer rely on support from the council of nine to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:52:40-08:00","id":1189902,"title":"","content":"Can anyone think of any situations in which the two <i>would </i>have gotten along and collaborated? Because such a thing would be a unique and unrepeatable symbol of a singular time in Tradition history. (Also because I'm considering running a Roaring 20's game)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T12:05:35-08:00","id":1189966,"title":"","content":"Both are great travelers. You could have a team of Tradition missionaries, trying to get more Crafts into the group. Batini and Etherite approach would be very different but, as the Traditions know very well, that makes the team more versatile.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, since Etherites were big on colonization, and consequently deployed into many of the covert Technocratical opperations on &quot;exotic&quot; places, they could give intel to the Batini to better defend their middle eastern resources against their former coleagues, or even make a joint opperation to counter these efforts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T12:11:48-08:00","id":1189970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1189858-the-early-20th-century-the-sons-of-ether-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1189966#post1189966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both are great travelers. You could have a team of Tradition missionaries, trying to get more Crafts into the group. Batini and Etherite approach would be very different but, as the Traditions know very well, that makes the team more versatile.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, since Etherites were big on colonization, and consequently deployed into many of the covert Technocratical opperations on &quot;exotic&quot; places, they could give intel to the Batini to better defend their middle eastern resources against their former coleagues, or even make a joint opperation to counter these efforts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are both absolutely amazing ideas. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T15:11:32-08:00","id":1190020,"title":"","content":"I think your basic reading works. But lets remember the collapse of the Ottoman state places large chunks of the Middle East directly under Western rule. Granted this rule was short, but the Batini can't get over it.<br /> <br /> The Batini see themselves as the only true center of the world. Most other groups have had this slapped out of them. The Batini, like the Wu-Lung or the Technocracy, still maintains this illustion. So they would be disgusted to work with Etherites. The Etherites would see them as new partners to build bridges to. People whose respect they want to gain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T19:04:32-08:00","id":1190096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1189858-the-early-20th-century-the-sons-of-ether-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1189902#post1189902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone think of any situations in which the two <i>would </i>have gotten along and collaborated? Because such a thing would be a unique and unrepeatable symbol of a singular time in Tradition history. (Also because I'm considering running a Roaring 20's game)</div> </div> </div> </div>A team up between period pulp heroes Doc Eon (or his WW1 counterpart) and Sir David Tinners (an homage to Laurence of Arabia and El Borak)?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T19:05:34-08:00","id":1190097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1189858-the-early-20th-century-the-sons-of-ether-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1190096#post1190096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A team up between period pulp heroes Doc Eon (or his WW1 counterpart) and Sir David Tinners (an homage to Laurence of Arabia and El Borak)?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why didn't I think of that!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T01:14:19-08:00","id":1190172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1189858-the-early-20th-century-the-sons-of-ether-and-the-ahl-i-batin?p=1189902#post1189902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone think of any situations in which the two <i>would </i>have gotten along and collaborated? Because such a thing would be a unique and unrepeatable symbol of a singular time in Tradition history. (Also because I'm considering running a Roaring 20's game)</div> </div> </div> </div>If a nephandic technomancer were about to do something that would cause widespread bloodshed in the Middle East, I could see Batini grudgingly allowing the Eetherites to aid them. The Batini would be deeply condescending and any misstep by the Etherites would cause vast offense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}